Let \[B_1=\text{ball chosen from bag } B_1\] and \[R=\text{red ball is obtained}\] Using Bayes' theorem, \[P(B_1|R)=\frac{P(R|B_1)P(B_1)}{P(R)}\] Since one of the two bags is chosen at random, \[P(B_1)=P(B_2)=\frac{1}{2}\] Also, \[P(R|B_1)=\frac{7}{10}\] and \[P(R|B_2)=\frac{3}{10}\] Now, \[P(R)=P(R|B_1)P(B_1)+P(R|B_2)P(B_2)\] \[=\frac{7}{10}\times\frac{1}{2}
+\frac{3}{10}\times\frac{1}{2}\] \[=\frac{7+3}{20}
=\frac{10}{20}
=\frac{1}{2}\] Therefore, \[P(B_1|R)=
\frac{\frac{7}{10}\times\frac{1}{2}}{\frac{1}{2}}\] \[=\frac{7}{10}
=0.7\] \[\boxed{0.7}\]

